<title>USA: Freddie Mac to redeem $360 mln in debentures.</title>
<headline>Freddie Mac to redeem $360 mln in debentures.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Freddie Mac said Thursday that on June 18 it will redeem all outstanding amounts of eight debenture issues totaling $360 million as follows.</p>
<p>		     Interest     Maturity	 Cusip</p>
<p>  Principal	  Rate	   Date	   Number</p>
<p> $75 million	 8.00	 05/15/06	3134A0H88</p>
<p> $50 million	 6.95	 06/18/99	3134A0T51</p>
<p> $50 million	 7.47	 06/18/01	3134A0S86</p>
<p> $50 million	 7.00	 06/18/99	3134A0T77</p>
<p> $50 million	 7.345	06/11/01	3134A0Q70</p>
<p> $50 million	 8.00	 05/15/06	3134A0J37</p>
<p> $25 million	 8.00	 05/16/06	3134A0J45</p>
<p> $10 million	 8.00	 05/16/06	3134A0H96</p>
<p>Payment of principal plus interest accrued to the redemption date will be made to shareholders of record as of the close of business on June 17, 1997, Freddie Mac said.</p>
<p>Freddie Mac is a corporation chartered by Congress that buys mortgages from lenders and packages them into securities for investors.</p>
